    {
      "id": "claim_58a84c43c0474a958956586d160bcb27",
      "statement": "Chrome, Safari, and Firefox extensions are thin browser-specific adapters around the shared background-controller, which depends on injected adapter interfaces (StorageAdapter, ActionAdapter, PageReaderAdapter, PageActionAdapter, SetupAdapter, TimersAdapter, BrijioSocket); each browser supplies only concrete wiring while shared logic stays in @brijio/shared. Extensions connect only on explicit user action, authenticate with the pairing token, announce presence, and answer explicit requests without streaming ambient state.",
      "evidence": [
